    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the acceptance test passes.\n\nI implemented the public-holiday rule in the single place responsible for the business-day roll-forward, `BusinessDayAdjuster`:\n\n- Added the fixed 2026 holiday list as a constant `Set<LocalDate>`.\n- Replaced the weekend-only special-casing with a small `isBusinessDay` helper (weekend **or** holiday \u2192 not a business day) and a loop in `toBusinessDay` that rolls forward one day at a time until it reaches a non-holiday weekday. This correctly handles chained non-business days (e.g. a holiday adjacent to a weekend, or the consecutive 2026-12-25/2026-12-28 pair).\n\n`RegistrationDateAssigner` needed no logic change since it already delegates to `BusinessDayAdjuster`; I only updated its Javadoc (and the adjuster's) to reflect the holiday behavior. The `Tests run: 1 ... BUILD SUCCESS` confirms the suite is green.",
